  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nQ = 2.5 × P\n\nS = 60% of Q\n\nR = (P + Q + R + S) ÷ 4\n\nP + R = 4800\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nAverage = Sum ÷ Number of terms\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ Let P = 100\n\n⇒ Q = 2.5 × 100 = 250\n\n⇒ S = 60% × 250 = 150\n\n⇒ R = (100 + 250 + R + 150) ÷ 4\n\n⇒ R = (500 + R) ÷ 4\n\n⇒ 4R = 500 + R\n\n⇒ 3R = 500\n\n⇒ R = 500 ÷ 3\n\n⇒ P + R = 100 + 500/3 = 800/3\n\n⇒ Scaling factor = 4800 ÷ (800/3) = 4800 × 3 ÷ 800 = 18\n\n⇒ Actual R = (500/3) × 18\n\n⇒ Actual R = 3000\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 3000.**",
